  "name": "unabsorbed-fastest-channel",
  "title": "The fastest channel wins where the loss cannot absorb it",
  "statement": "If $v$ is the only maximizer of $F$ on $P$ (Hypothesis 0), and either the principal part is diagonal (Hypothesis 2) or every mixed monomial of $D$ has weighted degree at least 1, then $\\gamma = \\min(\\gamma_{\\mathrm{face}}, \\gamma_{\\mathrm{V.22}})$. It combines the guard of issue #31 with the refinement found on issue #33, after `loss-absorption` refuted the version with Hypothesis 0 alone.",
